{"content":[{"c":["DARKNESS"],"sourceClass":"h1","t":"p"},{"c":["Absence of light or brightness. Although the Bible seldom refers to literal darkness, a number of words translated “darkness” are used in a figurative or metaphorical sense."],"sourceClass":"fl","t":"p"},{"c":["When God created the world, there was no light until he commanded that light appear. He then made distinction between light and its opposite, darkness, which he called night (",{"href":"?bref=Gen.1.2,4-5,18","r":"Gen.1.2,4-5,18","rawR":"Gen.1.2,4-5,18","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Gen.1.2,4-5,18","value":"Gen.1.2,4-5,18"}],"t":"ref","v":"Gn 1:2, 4-5, 18"},"). Literal darkness is also mentioned in the account of the plagues God inflicted on Egypt; the ninth plague was an intense darkness that could be “felt” (",{"href":"?bref=Exod.10.21-23","r":"Exod.10.21-23","rawR":"Exod.10.21-23","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Exod.10.21-23","value":"Exod.10.21-23"}],"t":"ref","v":"Ex 10:21-23"},"). That darkness lasted three days and was selective; wherever Egyptians were, it was dark, but where the Israelites were, there was light. The Israelites left Egypt accompanied by a cloud that separated them from their enemy, evidently giving light to the Israelites but making darkness for the Egyptians (",{"href":"?bref=Exod.14.20","r":"Exod.14.20","rawR":"Exod.14.20","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Exod.14.20","value":"Exod.14.20"}],"t":"ref","v":"Ex 14:20"},"). The Bible notes that thieves or adulterers are likely to do their evil deeds in the dark or at night (",{"href":"?bref=Job.24.16-17","r":"Job.24.16-17","rawR":"Job.24.16-17","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Job.24.16-17","value":"Job.24.16-17"}],"t":"ref","v":"Jb 24:16-17"},")."],"sourceClass":"","t":"p"},{"c":["In the NT “darkness” is used twice in its literal sense. At the crucifixion of Jesus, for a three-hour period from noon to three o’clock, there was not light (",{"href":"?bref=Matt.27.45","r":"Matt.27.45","rawR":"Matt.27.45","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Matt.27.45","value":"Matt.27.45"}],"t":"ref","v":"Mt 27:45"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Mark.15.33","r":"Mark.15.33","rawR":"Mark.15.33","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Mark.15.33","value":"Mark.15.33"}],"t":"ref","v":"Mk 15:33"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Luke.23.44","r":"Luke.23.44","rawR":"Luke.23.44","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Luke.23.44","value":"Luke.23.44"}],"t":"ref","v":"Lk 23:44"},"). The other reference is to Christ’s second coming, when “the sun will be darkened, and the moon will not give its light” (",{"href":"?bref=Matt.24.29","r":"Matt.24.29","rawR":"Matt.24.29","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Matt.24.29","value":"Matt.24.29"}],"t":"ref","v":"Mt 24:29"},", ",{"c":["rsv"],"sourceClass":"sc","t":"span"},")."],"sourceClass":"","t":"p"},{"c":["Several biblical passages speak of a darkness surrounding God, evidently moving from a literal sense of absence of light to a more profound meaning. God spoke to Moses on Mt Sinai in a dense, black cloud (",{"href":"?bref=Exod.20.21","r":"Exod.20.21","rawR":"Exod.20.21","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Exod.20.21","value":"Exod.20.21"}],"t":"ref","v":"Ex 20:21"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Deut.4.11","r":"Deut.4.11","rawR":"Deut.4.11","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Deut.4.11","value":"Deut.4.11"}],"t":"ref","v":"Dt 4:11"},") or from the darkness (",{"href":"?bref=Deut.5.23","r":"Deut.5.23","rawR":"Deut.5.23","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Deut.5.23","value":"Deut.5.23"}],"t":"ref","v":"Dt 5:23"},"). Darkness is pictured as a shelter or cloak around God (",{"href":"?bref=2Sam.22.12","r":"2Sam.22.12","rawR":"2Sam.22.12","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"2Sam.22.12","value":"2Sam.22.12"}],"t":"ref","v":"2 Sm 22:12"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Ps.18.11","r":"Ps.18.11","rawR":"Ps.18.11","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Ps.18.11","value":"Ps.18.11"}],"t":"ref","v":"Pss 18:11"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Ps.97.2","r":"Ps.97.2","rawR":"Ps.97.2","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Ps.97.2","value":"Ps.97.2"}],"t":"ref","v":"97:2"},"). God sets a boundary for light and darkness (",{"href":"?bref=Job.26.10","r":"Job.26.10","rawR":"Job.26.10","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Job.26.10","value":"Job.26.10"}],"t":"ref","v":"Jb 26:10"},"), brings darkness (",{"href":"?bref=Ps.104.20","r":"Ps.104.20","rawR":"Ps.104.20","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Ps.104.20","value":"Ps.104.20"}],"t":"ref","v":"Pss 104:20"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Ps.105.28","r":"Ps.105.28","rawR":"Ps.105.28","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Ps.105.28","value":"Ps.105.28"}],"t":"ref","v":"105:28"},"), and creates light and darkness (",{"href":"?bref=Isa.45.7","r":"Isa.45.7","rawR":"Isa.45.7","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Isa.45.7","value":"Isa.45.7"}],"t":"ref","v":"Is 45:7"},"). God dwells in thick darkness (",{"href":"?bref=1Kgs.8.12","r":"1Kgs.8.12","rawR":"1Kgs.8.12","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"1Kgs.8.12","value":"1Kgs.8.12"}],"t":"ref","v":"1 Kgs 8:12"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=2Chr.6.1","r":"2Chr.6.1","rawR":"2Chr.6.1","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"2Chr.6.1","value":"2Chr.6.1"}],"t":"ref","v":"2 Chr 6:1"},"), and thick darkness is under his feet (",{"href":"?bref=2Sam.22.10","r":"2Sam.22.10","rawR":"2Sam.22.10","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"2Sam.22.10","value":"2Sam.22.10"}],"t":"ref","v":"2 Sm 22:10"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Ps.18.9","r":"Ps.18.9","rawR":"Ps.18.9","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Ps.18.9","value":"Ps.18.9"}],"t":"ref","v":"Ps 18:9"},")."],"sourceClass":"","t":"p"},{"c":["Most figurative references to darkness appear in poetic material, such as Job, Psalms, and Isaiah. Generally, such darkness depicts ignorance about God’s will. Knowledge of God is “light”; hence, lack of such knowledge is “darkness” (",{"href":"?bref=Job.12.24-25","r":"Job.12.24-25","rawR":"Job.12.24-25","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Job.12.24-25","value":"Job.12.24-25"}],"t":"ref","v":"Jb 12:24-25"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Matt.4.16","r":"Matt.4.16","rawR":"Matt.4.16","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Matt.4.16","value":"Matt.4.16"}],"t":"ref","v":"Mt 4:16"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=John.1.5","r":"John.1.5","rawR":"John.1.5","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"John.1.5","value":"John.1.5"}],"t":"ref","v":"Jn 1:5"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=John.8.12","r":"John.8.12","rawR":"John.8.12","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"John.8.12","value":"John.8.12"}],"t":"ref","v":"8:12"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=John.12.35,46","r":"John.12.35,46","rawR":"John.12.35,46","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"John.12.35,46","value":"John.12.35,46"}],"t":"ref","v":"12:35, 46"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=1Jn.1.5","r":"1Jn.1.5","rawR":"1Jn.1.5","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"1Jn.1.5","value":"1Jn.1.5"}],"t":"ref","v":"1 Jn 1:5"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=1Jn.2.8-9,11","r":"1Jn.2.8-9,11","rawR":"1Jn.2.8-9,11","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"1Jn.2.8-9,11","value":"1Jn.2.8-9,11"}],"t":"ref","v":"2:8-9, 11"},")."],"sourceClass":"","t":"p"},{"c":["Job spoke of darkness as equivalent to nothingness (",{"href":"?bref=Job.3.4-6","r":"Job.3.4-6","rawR":"Job.3.4-6","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Job.3.4-6","value":"Job.3.4-6"}],"t":"ref","v":"Jb 3:4-6"},"). In other references darkness stands for death, a land of shadows and gloom, the dwelling place of the dead far from the light of day (",{"href":"?bref=Job.10.21-22","r":"Job.10.21-22","rawR":"Job.10.21-22","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Job.10.21-22","value":"Job.10.21-22"}],"t":"ref","v":"Jb 10:21-22"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Job.15.24","r":"Job.15.24","rawR":"Job.15.24","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Job.15.24","value":"Job.15.24"}],"t":"ref","v":"15:24"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Job.17.12-13","r":"Job.17.12-13","rawR":"Job.17.12-13","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Job.17.12-13","value":"Job.17.12-13"}],"t":"ref","v":"17:12-13"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Job.18.18","r":"Job.18.18","rawR":"Job.18.18","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Job.18.18","value":"Job.18.18"}],"t":"ref","v":"18:18"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Eccl.6.4","r":"Eccl.6.4","rawR":"Eccl.6.4","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Eccl.6.4","value":"Eccl.6.4"}],"t":"ref","v":"Eccl 6:4"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Eccl.11.8","r":"Eccl.11.8","rawR":"Eccl.11.8","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Eccl.11.8","value":"Eccl.11.8"}],"t":"ref","v":"11:8"},")."],"sourceClass":"","t":"p"},{"c":["Darkness frequently stands for distress and anxiety, or for the confusion and destruction experienced by the wicked (",{"href":"?bref=Gen.15.12","r":"Gen.15.12","rawR":"Gen.15.12","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Gen.15.12","value":"Gen.15.12"}],"t":"ref","v":"Gn 15:12"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Job.5.14","r":"Job.5.14","rawR":"Job.5.14","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Job.5.14","value":"Job.5.14"}],"t":"ref","v":"Jb 5:14"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Job.12.25","r":"Job.12.25","rawR":"Job.12.25","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Job.12.25","value":"Job.12.25"}],"t":"ref","v":"12:25"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Job.15.22,30","r":"Job.15.22,30","rawR":"Job.15.22,30","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Job.15.22,30","value":"Job.15.22,30"}],"t":"ref","v":"15:22, 30"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Job.19.8","r":"Job.19.8","rawR":"Job.19.8","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Job.19.8","value":"Job.19.8"}],"t":"ref","v":"19:8"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Job.22.11","r":"Job.22.11","rawR":"Job.22.11","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Job.22.11","value":"Job.22.11"}],"t":"ref","v":"22:11"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Ps.35.6","r":"Ps.35.6","rawR":"Ps.35.6","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Ps.35.6","value":"Ps.35.6"}],"t":"ref","v":"Pss 35:6"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Ps.107.10,14","r":"Ps.107.10,14","rawR":"Ps.107.10,14","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Ps.107.10,14","value":"Ps.107.10,14"}],"t":"ref","v":"107:10, 14"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Eccl.5.17","r":"Eccl.5.17","rawR":"Eccl.5.17","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Eccl.5.17","value":"Eccl.5.17"}],"t":"ref","v":"Eccl 5:17"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Isa.5.30","r":"Isa.5.30","rawR":"Isa.5.30","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Isa.5.30","value":"Isa.5.30"}],"t":"ref","v":"Is 5:30"},"). Moral depravity is sometimes described as darkness (",{"href":"?bref=Pr.2.13","r":"Pr.2.13","rawR":"Pr.2.13","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Pr.2.13","value":"Pr.2.13"}],"t":"ref","v":"Prv 2:13"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Pr.4.19","r":"Pr.4.19","rawR":"Pr.4.19","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Pr.4.19","value":"Pr.4.19"}],"t":"ref","v":"4:19"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Isa.5.20","r":"Isa.5.20","rawR":"Isa.5.20","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Isa.5.20","value":"Isa.5.20"}],"t":"ref","v":"Is 5:20"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Isa.60.2","r":"Isa.60.2","rawR":"Isa.60.2","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Isa.60.2","value":"Isa.60.2"}],"t":"ref","v":"60:2"},"). In the NT darkness is generally a metaphor of moral depravity and spiritual ignorance (",{"href":"?bref=Matt.4.16","r":"Matt.4.16","rawR":"Matt.4.16","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Matt.4.16","value":"Matt.4.16"}],"t":"ref","v":"Mt 4:16"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Matt.6.23","r":"Matt.6.23","rawR":"Matt.6.23","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Matt.6.23","value":"Matt.6.23"}],"t":"ref","v":"6:23"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Luke.1.79","r":"Luke.1.79","rawR":"Luke.1.79","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Luke.1.79","value":"Luke.1.79"}],"t":"ref","v":"Lk 1:79"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Luke.11.35","r":"Luke.11.35","rawR":"Luke.11.35","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Luke.11.35","value":"Luke.11.35"}],"t":"ref","v":"11:35"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Luke.22.53","r":"Luke.22.53","rawR":"Luke.22.53","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Luke.22.53","value":"Luke.22.53"}],"t":"ref","v":"22:53"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Rom.2.19","r":"Rom.2.19","rawR":"Rom.2.19","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Rom.2.19","value":"Rom.2.19"}],"t":"ref","v":"Rom 2:19"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Col.1.13","r":"Col.1.13","rawR":"Col.1.13","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Col.1.13","value":"Col.1.13"}],"t":"ref","v":"Col 1:13"},")."],"sourceClass":"","t":"p"},{"c":["A major theme of OT prophets was the Day of the Lord, often associated with darkness (",{"href":"?bref=Ezek.32.8","r":"Ezek.32.8","rawR":"Ezek.32.8","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Ezek.32.8","value":"Ezek.32.8"}],"t":"ref","v":"Ez 32:8"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Joel.2.2,31","r":"Joel.2.2,31","rawR":"Joel.2.2,31","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Joel.2.2,31","value":"Joel.2.2,31"}],"t":"ref","v":"Jl 2:2, 31"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Amos.5.18,20","r":"Amos.5.18,20","rawR":"Amos.5.18,20","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Amos.5.18,20","value":"Amos.5.18,20"}],"t":"ref","v":"Am 5:18, 20"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Zeph.1.15","r":"Zeph.1.15","rawR":"Zeph.1.15","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Zeph.1.15","value":"Zeph.1.15"}],"t":"ref","v":"Zep 1:15"},"). The NT also links darkness with judgment in connection with Christ’s second coming (",{"href":"?bref=Matt.8.12","r":"Matt.8.12","rawR":"Matt.8.12","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Matt.8.12","value":"Matt.8.12"}],"t":"ref","v":"Mt 8:12"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Matt.22.13","r":"Matt.22.13","rawR":"Matt.22.13","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Matt.22.13","value":"Matt.22.13"}],"t":"ref","v":"22:13"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Matt.25.30","r":"Matt.25.30","rawR":"Matt.25.30","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Matt.25.30","value":"Matt.25.30"}],"t":"ref","v":"25:30"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=2Pet.2.17","r":"2Pet.2.17","rawR":"2Pet.2.17","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"2Pet.2.17","value":"2Pet.2.17"}],"t":"ref","v":"2 Pt 2:17"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Jude.1.6,13","r":"Jude.1.6,13","rawR":"Jude.1.6,13","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Jude.1.6,13","value":"Jude.1.6,13"}],"t":"ref","v":"Jude 1:6, 13"},"). Those who come to know God are said to come out of darkness (",{"href":"?bref=Isa.9.2","r":"Isa.9.2","rawR":"Isa.9.2","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Isa.9.2","value":"Isa.9.2"}],"t":"ref","v":"Is 9:2"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Isa.29.18","r":"Isa.29.18","rawR":"Isa.29.18","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Isa.29.18","value":"Isa.29.18"}],"t":"ref","v":"29:18"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Isa.42.7","r":"Isa.42.7","rawR":"Isa.42.7","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Isa.42.7","value":"Isa.42.7"}],"t":"ref","v":"42:7"},"); darkness cannot be a hiding place from God (",{"href":"?bref=Job.34.22","r":"Job.34.22","rawR":"Job.34.22","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Job.34.22","value":"Job.34.22"}],"t":"ref","v":"Jb 34:22"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Ps.139.11-12","r":"Ps.139.11-12","rawR":"Ps.139.11-12","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Ps.139.11-12","value":"Ps.139.11-12"}],"t":"ref","v":"Ps 139:11-12"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Isa.29.15","r":"Isa.29.15","rawR":"Isa.29.15","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Isa.29.15","value":"Isa.29.15"}],"t":"ref","v":"Is 29:15"},")."],"sourceClass":"","t":"p"},{"c":[{"c":["See also"],"sourceClass":"ital","t":"span"}," ",{"href":"?item=Light_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","id":"Light_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","rawId":"Light_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","t":"link","v":"Light"},"."],"sourceClass":"","t":"p"}],"format":"bsb-study-dictionary-v2","id":"Darkness","provenance":{"archiveSha256":"10758ea00dbea7540f9337e43e59c8e4000295c1261e3426bab6f31c31dcff5b","release":"1.6","sourceCitationReferences":[{"anchorText":"Gn 1:2, 4-5, 18","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Gen.1.2,4-5,18","rawQueryValue":"Gen.1.2,4-5,18","sourceRefExact":"Gen.1.2,4-5,18"},{"anchorText":"Ex 10:21-23","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Exod.10.21-23","rawQueryValue":"Exod.10.21-23","sourceRefExact":"Exod.10.21-23"},{"anchorText":"Ex 14:20","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Exod.14.20","rawQueryValue":"Exod.14.20","sourceRefExact":"Exod.14.20"},{"anchorText":"Jb 24:16-17","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Job.24.16-17","rawQueryValue":"Job.24.16-17","sourceRefExact":"Job.24.16-17"},{"anchorText":"Mt 27:45","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Matt.27.45","rawQueryValue":"Matt.27.45","sourceRefExact":"Matt.27.45"},{"anchorText":"Mk 15:33","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Mark.15.33","rawQueryValue":"Mark.15.33","sourceRefExact":"Mark.15.33"},{"anchorText":"Lk 23:44","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Luke.23.44","rawQueryValue":"Luke.23.44","sourceRefExact":"Luke.23.44"},{"anchorText":"Mt 24:29","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Matt.24.29","rawQueryValue":"Matt.24.29","sourceRefExact":"Matt.24.29"},{"anchorText":"Ex 20:21","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Exod.20.21","rawQueryValue":"Exod.20.21","sourceRefExact":"Exod.20.21"},{"anchorText":"Dt 4:11","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Deut.4.11","rawQueryValue":"Deut.4.11","sourceRefExact":"Deut.4.11"},{"anchorText":"